# Non-secret config — defaults also baked into the code.
PORT='9416'
HOST='127.0.0.1'
DATA_DIR='./data'

# Workhorse model: problem generation, hints, session plans, primers, lessons,
# and the per-submit coaching brief. Everything that fires on a cadence the
# user doesn't control.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL='claude-sonnet-5'

# Teaching model: the tutor chat ONLY (POST /api/ask) — one call per question
# actually asked, the highest-value/lowest-frequency call in the app. Runs
# adaptive thinking so the model reasons about HOW to explain before answering.
ANTHROPIC_CHAT_MODEL='claude-opus-5'

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Anthropic API key — DO NOT PUT IT IN .env
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app asks for it in the browser on first run and stores it in the SQLite
# database, where it is checked against Anthropic before it is saved and where
# nothing can truncate it. That is the supported way in.
#
# The variable IS read, and if it is set it wins over the stored key — which is
# what a systemd deploy uses, supplying it through the unit rather than through
# this file. The reason it must not live here is mechanical rather than
# stylistic: some secret-management tooling rewrites .env with O_TRUNC on every
# deploy, so a key typed into this file can vanish without a word. See bin/setup
# and src/server/services/apikey.service.ts.
#
# And if you are pointing codegrind at a model you run yourself (below), you do
# not need an Anthropic key at all — nothing will ask you for one.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=''

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Running on something other than Claude
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything above keeps working exactly as it does today; these are opt-in, and
# every field is read at startup. Leave them unset for Anthropic.
#
# The provider for the workhorse calls: 'anthropic' (default) or
# 'openai-compatible' (llama.cpp, llama-swap, vLLM, Ollama, LM Studio, or any
# hosted endpoint speaking /v1/chat/completions).
# CODEGRIND_PROVIDER='openai-compatible'
#
# Where that endpoint is, INCLUDING the version segment. QWEN_URL is accepted as
# a fallback for boxes that already export one.
# CODEGRIND_ENDPOINT='http://127.0.0.1:9600/v1'
#
# The model id, exactly as the endpoint advertises it in /v1/models. There is no
# default and there deliberately never will be: picking one for you is how a
# router hands the job to whatever happens to be cheapest to load.
# CODEGRIND_MODEL='my-local-model-q8'
#
# The tutor. Unset means "match the workhorse" — a local install stays local,
# with no key and no spend. Set these to keep the tutor on Claude while the rest
# runs locally (or the reverse).
# CODEGRIND_CHAT_PROVIDER='anthropic'
# CODEGRIND_CHAT_MODEL='claude-opus-5'
#
# A bearer token for the endpoint, if it wants one. Most local fleets do not.
# CODEGRIND_API_KEY=''
#
# Model ids this install must NEVER send work to, comma-separated. codegrind
# cannot know a router's topology: an id in /v1/models can be mapped onto a CPU
# on this very machine, where a big model will fight the rest of the box for
# cores. On one deploy that id was simply the un-suffixed variant of the good
# one, and it was observed starving a media server's transcoder. Denied ids are
# filtered out of the in-app model picker as well as refused at call time.
# CODEGRIND_MODEL_DENY='my-local-model-cpu'
#
# The most output tokens any single call may ask a local endpoint for. Unset
# means 8000, which is a measurement rather than a guess: a real generated
# problem is 976-5337 output tokens, while a generation that degenerates into
# repetition runs to whatever budget it is handed — so the budget's job here is
# to arrive sooner (144s instead of 293s for the same discarded problem). Raise
# it if your model genuinely writes bigger problems and you see good ones cut
# off; 0 turns the ceiling off and sends each call site's own number.
# CODEGRIND_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS='8000'
